# Entity and state language

A domain identifies an entity family, such as `light`. A device class gives more specific meaning, such as a door sensor. A state is the value Home Assistant holds; attributes add related information. None of these facts alone proves that a physical device was inspected or an action completed.

Use the entity's actual native label and supplied name. Explain the meaning with its domain, device class, relevant unit and time. Do not substitute a global “on”, “off”, “failed” or “offline” label for the source's more precise state.

