## Read identifiers according to their role

| Kind | Example | How to use it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Entity ID | `light.nains_reading_lamp` | A complete synthetic entity identifier; use the actual configured ID in a real instruction |
| Domain | `light` | An entity family, not a complete entity ID |
| Raw state | `on` | Interpret through domain and device-class context |
| Attribute property | `hvac_action` | A key within the state record, not an entity ID |
| Attribute value | `heating` | A value of a specified attribute, distinct from a selected mode |
| Device-class translation key | `door` | The class-specific label mapping for the named domain |
| Translation fallback key | `_` | An internal default translation entry; do not copy it as an entity ID or device-class setting |

The tables below are **English source-label references**, not new translations. Home Assistant selects the native language and supported labels. Vendor-specific values may be supplied dynamically and are outside this fixed list.

