## Use the reference safely in authored content

Keep `unknown`, `unavailable` and real zero values distinct. Use the actual source label where available, then add enough context for the task. A lock can report Locked without an independent physical check; a climate entity can be set to Heat while its current action is Idle. A helper can store On without operating a device.

For an unfamiliar integration-specific state, read that integration's documentation and source. Preserve the supplied value until its meaning is established. Do not invent a translation, apply another device's meaning or conceal the unknown value behind a generic success label.

The [terminology register](../reference/ha-terminology.json) records every source pointer, key role and coverage denominator. Use the [entity-state specification](../home-assistant/entity-state.html) for freshness and missing data, and [action results](../home-assistant/action-results.html) for requests and confirmation. Source mappings do not certify an installed control or a physical result.
